      "question": "Are I bonds worth it when inflation is high?",
      "answer": "I bonds provide purchasing power protection because their composite interest rate adjusts for inflation every six months. The rate for bonds issued between May 1, 2026 and October 31, 2026 is 4.26 percent, which includes a 0.90 percent fixed rate that remains active for the 30-year life of the bond."
    },
